I first started playing Nethack sometime around 1997 or 1998, but
never "seriously"... I don't think I ever got to a quest level, let
alone beat one.  (I remember once getting a wish, and having no idea
what to type at the prompt, answered "a good sword".)  After a nearly-
decade-long hiatus, I started playing more seriously (and spoiledly)
about a month ago.  I had a good run with a Valkyrie a couple weeks
ago, but I think you'll be able to tell how I ruined that character
when you look at the #names in my equipment dump below :)  This was
actually my first attempt playing Samurai, at least since the 1990s.
Game played was on nethack.alt.org under username "robomancer".
Thanks a bunch to the folks on #nethack for advice and support :)

All told, the game lasted over a week -- I started on 2008-10-03 and
ascended on 2008-10-12.  So apologies in advance for a long post.

Probably the closest I came to dying was in the early game -- stepped
on a magic trap on the Oracle level and found myself surrounded by
more baddies than I could handle.  Thankfully there was a room only a
few steps away; I was able to scramble in and lock the door behind me
to get some breathing room.  Stairs down were nearby, but that wasn't
much help as the floor below was also full of nasties.  So after
healing up I went back upstairs to engage.  Using the doorway
intelligently, I was able to pick them off one-by-one, and eventually
made it back into the Oracle room at about 1/3 HP... where I was
promptly attacked by a gargoyle.   After dancing around and spending
all my available ranged attacks on the gargoyle, I decided to engage
in honorable melee combat, which was stupid :)  I failed to write E
twice so I was very lucky to escape the battle with 2 HP remaining.
Ran upstairs and spent some time levelling up before I went back to
Oracle...

Mines and Sokoban were pretty uneventful (got two magic markers in
Mines, which would be the only ones I found in the game, and
"oReflection from Soko).  At some point I #dipped for Excalibur and
dual-wielded Excalibur and the starting katana until the quest.  Even
after Minetown and Sokoban, I had found no gloves.  Thanks to another
magic trap, I ended up blinded when I knew there were cockatrices
around, which led to another scary fight where I had to be very very
careful.  Lack of decent gloves would be a problem throughout the
game; I eventually found yugake but the only magical gloves I
encountered in the whole game were fumbling.  At some point my dog
stepped on a polymorph trap and became a silver dragon; he then killed
a priestess of Susanowo on the level below Oracle, which let me
convert the altar.  Draco-Goggie later ate a chameleon corpse, which
turned him into a lichen.  I had no way of polying him back into
anything mobile so had to leave him there.  Later I accidentally
killed him by running into him while blind :(

Found Ludios for my first time ever; with my newfound riches I was
able to buy 9 points of protection from Minetown priest.  Got a wish
from a throne at some point (maybe Ludios?), got +3 GDSM.

Quest was pretty uneventful, except that I didn't manage to paralyze/
sleep Ashikaga-san.  I also didn't realize he would teleport back to
me after teleporting away, so there was a lot more melee than I
expected.  He got at least a couple hits on me before I realized I
should probably equip the "oLS.  He then bisected me once and the "oLS
went poof... he got a few more hits on my with the Tsurugi before I
finally managed to kill him, so I'm very lucky to have escaped the
fight alive.

Throughout the game I had a ton of enchant weapon scrolls; I ended up
enchanting Tsurugi to +7, which is what I wielded up through the end
of the castle.  I found a /oPoly at some point and managed to poly
myself a BoH.  Found =oTC, so ate a bunch of leprechauns until I got
teleportitis.  After losing 3 int to a mind flayer and getting
amnesia, decided to write a scroll of geno for h (had already genoed
L).  With the castle wand I wished for +3 boots of speed, and spent 3
wishes getting Frost Brand.  After conferring with the folks in
#nethack, decided it wasn't worth spending one of the remaining wishes
to upgrade yugake to gauntlets of power.  At this point I wrote a
bunch of enchant armor scrolls (emptying one marker and part of
another), blessed them all, and enchanted my armor to pretty much the
final levels it'd obtain.  My AC was around -37 at this point and
would eventually peak at -41. Also managed to get Frost Brand and the
starting katana to +7.  I'd also gained 4 scrolls of genocide from
polymorphing; I blessed 3 for some nurse dancing and used the
remaining one to geno m in hopes of getting good stuff from Orcus-town
(I didn't).

I had a fair number of magic mapping scrolls, so Gehennom was fairly
painless.  Vlad was trivial of course.  I managed to nail Orcus with c
corpse before he got a single attack in; turned out he actually had
two /oDeath in his inventory, the only two I found in the whole game.
Found the vibrating square, cleaned out the moats around the Wizards
towers, then went up to my stash to do some alchemy and get together
all the scrolls, potions, tools, etc. I'd need for the ascension run.
Made it past Rodney's zoo quite easily due to a ring of conflict I'd
just found.  At the moat around Rodney's lair I embarassingly learned
that I'd completely forgotten to bring wands for my ascension run, and
had in fact left ALL of them in my stash.  Went back up to get them,
and back down again, then killed Rodney with /oDeath and got the
book.  Performed invocation; Sanctum was easy due to conflict.  Had
huge problems with the mysterious force in Gehennom (whee, lawful).  I
didn't count but I'm guessing I was affected at least 10 times,
including 3 at the upstair in Orcus-town.  Rodney spawned 2 more times
in Gehennom; /oDeathed him each time.  After Orcus-town I wasn't
affected by mysterious force at all, so it went quickly from then on.

Made a brief stop by my stash just to dump some spent wands and grab
new ones, then started for the planes.  Rodney appeared for the last
time at Plane of Earth and got promptly /oDeathed.  Earth and Fire
were trivial; I put on =oConflict again for Air, which made it take a
long time (due to too many messages about monsters killing each other)
but also made it pretty easy.  Plane of Water took forever, possibly
because I didn't understand the mechanics.  Ended up deciding to just
stay in a bubble and ride it around, I eventually found the portal
completely by luck/accident.

Still had conflict on when entering Astral, so I was greeted by a
hostile angel.  Death was at the center altar, so I killed him first.
Teleported everyone else out of my way and made it to the altar.  It
turned out to be chaotic.  At that point I had to decide... helm of
opposite alignment or not?  I consider it somewhat of a cop-out to
switch at the last moment, but in the end my fear of YASD won out and
so I decided to wish for the helm.  I repaid Susanowo for killing his
priestess and converting his altar by offering up the Amulet of
Yendor...

I ended up with place #1608 on the NAO top-2000 list with 4486206
points.  Didn't think I'd score so high, but I guess I *had*
overprepared for the end-game, and also brought all my gems with
me :)  I also accidentally got a conduct -- polyselfless -- which is
relatively lame as conducts go, but it was a nice surprise
nonetheless.

